1px solid #ddd;'>British wellness, aromatherapy</td></tr><tr><td style='padding: 0.75rem; border: 1px solid #ddd;'><strong>This Works</strong></td><td style='padding: 0.75rem; border: 1px solid #ddd;'>PR Application</td><td style='padding: 0.75rem; border: 1px solid #ddd;'>3K+</td><td style='padding: 0.75rem; border: 1px solid #ddd;'>Sleep wellness, UK brand</td></tr><tr><td style='padding: 0.75rem; border: 1px solid #ddd;'><strong>Huel</strong></td><td style='padding: 0.75rem; border: 1px solid #ddd;'>Affiliate + Gifting</td><td style='padding: 0.75rem; border: 1px solid #ddd;'>5K+</td><td style='padding: 0.75rem; border: 1px solid #ddd;'>UK-founded, complete nutrition</td></tr></table><h2 id='uk-pr-tips' style='color: #333; font-size: 1.8rem;'>Tips for UK Creators Getting PR Packages</h2><p>Getting PR as a UK creator has unique advantages and challenges:</p><h3 style='color: #26A69A; font-size: 1.3rem;'>Advantages for UK Creators</h3><ul style='list-style: disc; padding-left: 1.5rem;'><li><strong>Less competition:</strong> US-focused lists mean fewer UK creators applying to British brands</li><li><strong>Local authenticity:</strong> UK brands want content that resonates with British audiences</li><li><strong>Shipping is easier:</strong> No customs delays, cheaper for brands to ship within UK</li><li><strong>Time zone alignment:</strong> Same working hours as UK PR teams</li></ul><h3 style='color: #26A69A; font-size: 1.3rem;'>UK-Specific Pitch Tips</h3><ul style='list-style: disc; padding-left: 1.5rem;'><li><strong>Mention your UK location:</strong> \"Based in Manchester\" or \"London creator\" signals you're local</li><li><strong>Reference UK stores:</strong> \"I shop at Boots/Superdrug\" shows brand awareness</li><li><strong>Use British spelling:</strong> Colour not color, favourite not favorite in your pitches</li><li><strong>Know UK pricing:</strong> Reference pounds, not dollars, when discussing products</li><li><strong>Tag UK accounts:</strong> Many brands have separate UK Instagram accounts (@brand_uk)</li></ul><a href='/register/creator?utm_source=blog&utm_medium=organic&utm_campaign=uk-brands-that-send-pr-packages-2026' style='display: inline-block; background: #26A69A; color: white; padding: 0.75rem 1.5rem; border-radius: 4px; text-decoration: none; font-weight: 600; margin: 1rem 0;'>Create Your UK Creator Profile</a><h2 id='uk-pr-agencies' style='color: #333; font-size: 1.8rem;'>UK PR Agencies That Work with Micro-Influencers</h2><p>Many UK brands route their influencer gifting through PR agencies. These agencies represent multiple brands and are worth pitching directly:</p><table style='width: 100%; border-collapse: collapse; margin: 2rem 0;'><tr style='background: #f0f9f7;'><th style='padding: 0.75rem; border: 1px solid #ddd; text-align: left;'>Agency</th><th style='padding: 0.75rem; border: 1px solid #ddd; text-align: left;'>Speciality</th><th style='padding: 0.75rem; border: 1px solid #ddd; text-align: left;'>How to Apply</th></tr><tr><td style='padding: 0.75rem; border: 1px solid #ddd;'><strong>The Lifestyle Agency</strong></td><td style='padding: 0.75rem; border: 1px solid #ddd;'>Beauty, lifestyle brands</td><td style='padding: 0.75rem; border: 1px solid #ddd;'>Email with media kit</td></tr><tr><td style='padding: 0.75rem; border: 1px solid #ddd;'><strong>One Green Bean</strong></td><td style='padding: 0.75rem; border: 1px solid #ddd;'>Food, drink, FMCG</td><td style='padding: 0.75rem; border: 1px solid #ddd;'>Application form</td></tr><tr><td style='padding: 0.75rem; border: 1px solid #ddd;'><strong>Bottle PR</strong></td><td style='padding: 0.75rem; border: 1px solid #ddd;'>Beauty, wellness</td><td style='padding: 0.75rem; border: 1px solid #ddd;'>Email influencer team</td></tr><tr><td style='padding: 0.75rem; border: 1px solid #ddd;'><strong>Frank PR</strong></td><td style='padding: 0.75rem; border: 1px solid #ddd;'>Consumer brands</td><td style='padding: 0.75rem; border: 1px solid #ddd;'>Email with media kit</td></tr><tr><td style='padding: 0.75rem; border: 1px solid #ddd;'><strong>Talker Tailor</strong></td><td style='padding: 0.75rem; border: 1px solid #ddd;'>Lifestyle, interiors</td><td style='padding: 0.75rem; border: 1px solid #ddd;'>Email PR team</td></tr></table><h2 id='faq' style='color: #333; font-size: 1.8rem;'>FAQ</h2><div class='faq-section' style='margin: 2rem 0;'><div class='faq-item' style='margin-bottom: 1.5rem; padding: 1rem; background: #f8f9fa; border-radius: 8px;'><h4 style='color: #26A69A; margin-bottom: 0.5rem;'>Do UK brands only work with UK-based creators?</h4><p style='margin: 0;'>Most British brands prefer UK creators for practical reasons (shipping costs, local relevance, same time zone). However, many will work with EU creators or those with strong UK audiences. Being UK-based is definitely an advantage.</p></div><div class='faq-item' style='margin-bottom: 1.5rem; padding: 1rem; background: #f8f9fa; border-radius: 8px;'><h4 style='color: #26A69A; margin-bottom: 0.5rem;'>How many followers do I need for UK brand PR?</h4><p style='margin: 0;'>UK brands tend to be more micro-friendly than US brands. Many work with creators from 1K-5K followers. Revolution Beauty, Barry M, and Boohoo all accept creators with 1K-2K followers. Focus on engagement rate (3%+) over follower count.</p></div><div class='faq-item' style='margin-bottom: 1.5rem; padding: 1rem; background: #f8f9fa; border-radius: 8px;'><h4 style='color: #26A69A; margin-bottom: 0.5rem;'>Should I email UK brands in British English?</h4><p style='margin: 0;'>Yes. Use British spelling (colour, favourite, organised) and British terminology. It shows attention to detail and signals you understand their market. Small things like this make your pitch stand out.</p></div><div class='faq-item' style='margin-bottom: 1.5rem; padding: 1rem; background: #f8f9fa; border-radius: 8px;'><h4 style='color: #26A69A; margin-bottom: 0.5rem;'>Are UK PR packages different from US ones?</h4><p style='margin: 0;'>UK packages tend to be more curated and less \"PR haul\" style. British brands often send fewer products but higher quality selections. They're also more likely to include handwritten notes and branded packaging.</p></div><div class='faq-item' style='margin-bottom: 1.5rem; padding: 1rem; background: #f8f9fa; border-radius: 8px;'><h4 style='color: #26A69A; margin-bottom: 0.5rem;'>What's the best time to email UK PR teams?</h4><p style='margin: 0;'>Tuesday to Thursday, 9am-11am GMT. Avoid Mondays (inbox overwhelm) and Fridays (weekend mindset). UK PR teams typically work 9-5 GMT, so schedule your emails accordingly.</p></div></div><div class='cta-section' style='background: #f8f9fa; padding: 2rem; border-radius: 8px; margin-top: 2rem; text-align: center;'><h3 style='margin-bottom: 1rem;'>Ready to Get PR from British Brands?</h3><p style='margin-bottom: 1.5rem;'>Join UK creators already receiving brand offers on newcollab.</p><div style='display: flex; justify-content: center; gap: 1rem; margin-bottom: 1.5rem;'><div style='text-align: center;'><div style='font-size: 2rem; font-weight: bold; color: #26A69A;'>50+</div><div>UK Brands</div></div><div style='text-align: center;'><div style='font-size: 2rem; font-weight: bold; color: #26A69A;'>Direct</div><div>Contact Info</div></div><div style='text-align: center;'><div style='font-size: 2rem; font-weight: bold; color: #26A69A;'>Updated</div><div>Monthly</div></div></div><a href='/register/creator?utm_source=blog&utm_medium=organic&utm_campaign=uk-brands-that-send-pr-packages-2026' style='display: inline-block; background: #26A69A; color: white; padding: 1rem 2rem; border-radius: 4px; text-decoration: none; font-weight: 600; margin-bottom: 1rem; font-size: 1.1rem;'>Create Your Free Profile</a><p style='margin-top: 1rem; font-size: 0.9rem; color: #6c757d;'>Your UK location is your advantage. Use it.</p></div></div>",
